<mujoco model="k1_robocup_middle_scene">
  <!--
    RoboCup 2026 Humanoid Soccer League M-Field (former AdultSize), the field of
    the Middle Division the K1 plays in, for the vendored Booster K1 (see
    K1_22dof.xml / VENDORED.md). Identical to k1_scene_robocup.xml (KidSize)
    apart from the pitch, generated by generate_field.py from the HSL 2026
    rules (Law 1 "Dimensions"): field 14x9 m playing area + 1 m border, goal
    area 1x4 m, penalty area 3x6 m, penalty mark 2 m from the goal line,
    center circle diameter 3 m, corner arcs radius 0.5 m, lines 0.05 m. The
    rules allow a goal 2.4-2.6 m wide and 1.5-1.9 m high; this one is 2.5 m
    between the inner post edges (2.6 m post-center to post-center) with the
    crossbar at 1.8 m. The Middle Division plays with a FIFA size 3 or 4 ball;
    the ball below is still the KidSize one the Yolo model was trained on.
    Launch with `./b run sim/soccer --model models/k1/k1_scene_robocup_middle.xml`.

    Solver settings (timestep 0.001, Newton, impratio 10) come from the
    included K1_22dof.xml and are intentionally not overridden here.

    Ball body layout note: the "ball" body is declared at pos="0 0 0" with
    its sphere geom offset to pos="1.38 0 0.0785" (rather than putting that
    offset on the body itself). This is deliberate: K1_22dof.xml's own
    "ready"/"lying_front"/"lying_back" keyframes were authored with qpos
    sized for the bare robot (nq=29); once this scene adds the ball's
    freejoint (nq becomes 36), MuJoCo silently zero-pads the missing 7
    ball qpos entries in those inherited keyframes to (0,0,0,1,0,0,0)
    (verified: it pads with zero, not with the body's qpos0/pos attribute,
    and MuJoCo rejects two <key> elements sharing a name, so the keyframes
    cannot simply be redefined here). Zeroing the *body* frame and offsetting
    the *geom* means that zero-padded default is exactly the intended rest
    pose, so the ball lands at (1.38, 0, 0.0785) under all three inherited
    keyframes with no scene-level keyframe override required.

    A dedicated "kickoff" keyframe below places the robot at the match-start
    spawn pose (own half at x = -3.0, facing +x) using the same joint angles
    as "ready" (its own base height retuned to 0.555, like "ready" -- see
    VENDORED.md).
  -->
  <include file="K1_22dof.xml"/>

  <asset>
    <texture type="skybox" builtin="gradient" rgb1="0.35 0.55 0.75" rgb2="0 0 0" width="512" height="512"/>
    <texture name="grass_tex" type="2d" builtin="checker" rgb1="0.06 0.35 0.08" rgb2="0.05 0.30 0.07"
              width="300" height="300" mark="edge" markrgb="0.08 0.4 0.1"/>
    <material name="grass_mat" texture="grass_tex" texrepeat="22 16" texuniform="true" reflectance="0.05" specular="0.1"/>
    <material name="post_mat" rgba="0.95 0.95 0.95 1"/>
    <material name="ball_mat" rgba="0.85 0.25 0.05 1"/>
    <!-- NUpbr ball_001 asset (mesh normalised to unit radius in Blender, UVs preserved) -->
    <mesh name="ball_visual" file="ball_001.obj" scale="0.0785 0.0785 0.0785"/>
    <texture name="ball_tex" type="2d" file="meshes/ball_001_color.png"/>
    <material name="ball_tex_mat" texture="ball_tex" specular="0.3" shininess="0.4"/>
  </asset>

  <visual>
    <headlight ambient="0.35 0.35 0.35" diffuse="0.5 0.5 0.5" specular="0.2 0.2 0.2"/>
    <rgba haze="0.15 0.25 0.35 1"/>
  </visual>

  <worldbody>
    <light name="sun1" directional="true" pos="3 2 6" dir="-0.4 -0.3 -1" diffuse="0.7 0.7 0.65" specular="0.2 0.2 0.2" castshadow="true"/>
    <light name="sun2" directional="true" pos="-3 -2 6" dir="0.3 0.2 -1" diffuse="0.35 0.35 0.35" specular="0.05 0.05 0.05" castshadow="false"/>

